//@version=6
// LIVE TEST LEVEL 2c — MEASURE THE OCO LEG EXECUTING. SUPERVISED ONLY.
//
// WHY THIS EXISTS. Every L2 case relies on the native OCO bracket, and the census shows
// NO umbrella leg — neither TP nor SL — has ever been observed EXECUTING on DNSE in any
// run we have. l2b proved the bracket is PLACED and ARMS on the fill bar; it has never
// shown what the venue does when a leg actually triggers. That is the whole question here:
// on trigger, does the venue AMEND the child (same id, new price) or SPAWN a new id, is
// the other leg cancelled by the venue and when, and does a triggered stop-limit fill or
// rest unfilled. Until that is measured, the protection every fill-tier case depends on is
// a design we believe rather than a behaviour we have seen.
//
// SHAPE: l2b's, deliberately — a BREAKOUT stop entry at `higherHigh2` with the TP/SL
// derived from that TRIGGER (never from `close`: measured 2026-09-11 over 275 VN30F1M 15m
// bars, a close-derived TP sat BELOW the entry on 50.7% of bars). Reusing the shape keeps
// this comparable with the l2b evidence instead of introducing a second unvalidated
// vehicle.
//
// THREE DIFFERENCES FROM l2b, each one so a LEG CAN ACTUALLY EXECUTE:
//
//   1. ENTER-ONCE LATCH. l2b re-enters after every close, which is right for a latency
//      test and wrong here: repeated round-trips would leave several umbrellas and several
//      children in the record, and the grading question ("which id did the venue amend")
//      becomes unanswerable when there are four of each. The latch is set on the first
//      FILL, not on the first entry dispatch — so the resting entry still CHASES the
//      moving breakout while flat and unfilled, exactly as l2b does, and only the RE-ENTRY
//      after a completed round-trip is blocked. Setting it at dispatch instead would pin
//      the entry to the first bar's breakout level and it might never fill at all.
//
//   2. THE MAX-2-CANDLES FLATTEN IS REMOVED. In l2b it closed 13 of 39 episodes at two
//      bars. Here it would pre-empt the measurement in exactly the cases worth measuring:
//      a leg that has not triggered within two bars is the interesting one, and killing
//      the position there guarantees we never see the venue act.
//
//   3. THE BACKSTOP SCALES OFF THE SL LEG: `-(slPct + 0.25)`. l2b's fixed -0.3% sat
//      outside its fixed 0.2% bracket; here the legs are configurable, so the backstop has
//      to move with them. It is bounded by the SL and NOT by max(tp, sl), because the
//      backstop is loss-side only and the take-profit setting must not be allowed to
//      decide the loss limit. A fixed 0.25% margin keeps it clear of a working stop while
//      still bounding the loss tightly when the stop leg does NOT fill — which is the
//      failure this run exists to detect, so a fire here is the measurement, not a loss.
//
// TWO PLANNED RUNS, same file, inputs only:
//   run A, STOP-FAVOURED : slPct 0.05, tpPct 0.5  -> SL triggers; backstop -0.30%, ~6 pts
//   run B, TP-FAVOURED   : tpPct 0.05, slPct 0.3  -> TP triggers; backstop -0.55%, ~11 pts
// (points at a ~1985 index level; 1 point = 100,000 VND per contract)
// One leg is put close enough to the trigger that it should execute within a bar or two;
// the other is parked far away so it stays resting and its venue-side cancellation can be
// observed. The defaults below (tp 0.2 / sl 0.05) are the briefed values and are NOT
// either planned run — set the inputs explicitly per run.
//
// UNCHANGED GUARDS: 1 lot, pyramiding=0, `barstate.isrealtime` (warmup NEVER trades, so a
// plain `dnse:` backtest places ZERO trades and that is the offline proof), the pre-placed
// `strategy.exit` so #121 arms it on the fill bar, and the cancel-before-close ordering in
// the backstop so no resting leg can re-open exposure after a flatten.
//
// PRECONDITION: continuous session, FLAT account, operator watching, DNSE app open.
strategy("LIVE2c OCO leg execution", overlay=true, pyramiding=0, initial_capital=500000000,
     default_qty_type=strategy.fixed, default_qty_value=1,
     margin_long=18.48, margin_short=18.48,
     slippage=1,
     calc_on_every_tick=false, process_orders_on_close=false)

// --- configurable legs (percent off the entry TRIGGER) --------------------------------
tpPct = input.float(0.2,  "TP % off trigger", minval=0.01, step=0.01)
slPct = input.float(0.05, "SL % off trigger", minval=0.01, step=0.01)

// The backstop is LOSS-SIDE ONLY, so it must be bounded by the SL leg, never by the TP.
// An earlier draft used -3 x max(tpPct, slPct), which let the TAKE-PROFIT setting decide
// the loss limit: with run A at tp 0.5 that bounded the loss at -1.5%, about 30 points or
// 3,000,000 VND per contract, in exactly the scenario this run exists to detect — a stop
// leg that fails to fill. Bounding off the SL instead keeps the backstop a fixed 0.25%
// outside whichever stop is in force, so it never pre-empts a working stop, and a fire
// here IS the gap-through measurement rather than a loss.
//   run A (sl 0.05) -> -0.30%    run B (sl 0.3) -> -0.55%
// WRITTEN WITH NO PARENTHESES ON PURPOSE. Measured 2026-09-18: pine2pyne DROPS
// parentheses in this expression. `-(slPct + 0.25)` transpiled to `-slPct + 0.25`, and
// `0.0 - (slPct + 0.25)` transpiled to `0.0 - slPct + 0.25`. Both evaluate to +0.20 at
// sl 0.05 instead of -0.30 — a POSITIVE threshold, and since the test is
// `openPnlPct < DOUBLE_CHECK_PCT` the backstop would fire on the first bar of every
// position, cancel the bracket and flatten, destroying the measurement it protects.
// `-0.25 - slPct` needs no parentheses, so there are none to drop: it reads the same
// left-to-right in both languages. Verify against the GENERATED .py, never the .pine,
// after any edit to this line.
DOUBLE_CHECK_PCT = -0.25 - slPct

var float tpLevel   = na
var float slLevel   = na
var bool  hasTraded = false      // the ENTER-ONCE latch — set on the first FILL

higherHigh2 = high > high[1] ? high : high[1]

// Latch on the first FILL, not on the first dispatch. While flat and unfilled the entry
// keeps chasing (see note 1 above); once a position has existed, no further round-trip.
//
// BOTH CONDITIONS ARE REQUIRED, and `opentrades` ALONE IS NOT ENOUGH. Measured live
// 2026-09-18 (#159): trade 1 opened at 1994.8 and its stop filled at 1993.7 INSIDE bar
// 502. `strategy.opentrades` is only observable when the script runs, once per bar close,
// and order commit is deferred (CLAUDE.md: the count does not change until the NEXT bar
// after orders fill). So at bar 502's evaluation the entry had not filled, and at bar
// 503's the position was already closed — `opentrades` read 0 at BOTH boundaries, the
// latch never fired, the entry block re-issued, and a second position opened. It then sat
// unprotected for 66 s because an unrelated engine defect (#162) deferred its bracket.
//
// `closedtrades` increments on the close and PERSISTS, so it is the condition that
// survives a round-trip completing inside one bar — which is precisely the fast stop this
// vehicle exists to produce. The opentrades arm is kept for the ordinary multi-bar case.
if strategy.opentrades > 0 or strategy.closedtrades > 0
    hasTraded := true

// (1) the CHASING entry + its pre-placed native OCO bracket — LIVE bars only, once only.
if barstate.isrealtime and strategy.opentrades == 0 and not hasTraded
    tpLevel := higherHigh2 * (1.0 + tpPct / 100.0)
    slLevel := higherHigh2 * (1.0 - slPct / 100.0)
    strategy.entry("E", strategy.long, stop=higherHigh2, comment="STOP 1-lot")
    strategy.exit("X", from_entry="E", limit=tpLevel, stop=slLevel, oca_name="brk",
                  comment_profit="TP", comment_loss="SL")
    log.info("L2C ENTRY dispatch trigger={0} tp={1} sl={2} tpPct={3} slPct={4}",
             higherHigh2, tpLevel, slLevel, tpPct, slPct)

// (2) re-issue the pre-placed bracket while the position is open. No oca_type — Pine
//     strategy.exit has no such parameter and its legs already form a reduce group.
if strategy.opentrades > 0
    strategy.exit("X", from_entry="E", limit=tpLevel, stop=slLevel, oca_name="brk",
                  comment_profit="TP", comment_loss="SL")
    log.info("L2C EXIT reissue tp={0} sl={1} pos={2}",
             tpLevel, slLevel, strategy.position_size)

// (3) WHICH LEG CLOSED IT — the measurement this file exists for. exit_comment is TP or
//     SL as set above. Index is closedtrades-1; the count itself is never a valid index.
if strategy.position_size == 0 and strategy.position_size[1] != 0 and strategy.closedtrades > 0
    log.info("L2C CLOSED by={0} entry={1} exit={2} pnl={3}",
             strategy.closedtrades.exit_comment(strategy.closedtrades - 1),
             strategy.closedtrades.entry_price(strategy.closedtrades - 1),
             strategy.closedtrades.exit_price(strategy.closedtrades - 1),
             strategy.closedtrades.profit(strategy.closedtrades - 1))

// (4) DOUBLE-CHECK backstop, outermost. Cancel first so no resting leg can re-open
//     exposure after the flatten. PnL% is computed MANUALLY: strategy.opentrades
//     .profit_percent() reads 0.0 for an OPEN trade (measured 2026-09-11, profit went
//     0 -> -6 while profit_percent stayed 0.0000), which made this layer dead code.
//     entry_price and size ARE live on an open trade, so derive it from price. _bsDir
//     inverts it for a short, without which a losing short would report a gain.
_bsEntry = strategy.opentrades > 0 ? strategy.opentrades.entry_price(strategy.opentrades - 1) : 0.0
_bsSize  = strategy.opentrades > 0 ? strategy.opentrades.size(strategy.opentrades - 1) : 0.0
_bsDir   = _bsSize < 0 ? -1.0 : 1.0
_bsLive  = strategy.position_size != 0 and not na(_bsEntry) and _bsEntry != 0.0
openPnlPct = _bsLive ? (close - _bsEntry) / _bsEntry * 100.0 * _bsDir : 0.0
if strategy.position_size != 0 and openPnlPct < DOUBLE_CHECK_PCT
    strategy.cancel_all()
    strategy.close_all(comment="DOUBLECHECK")
    log.info("L2C BACKSTOP fired at {0} pct, threshold {1}", openPnlPct, DOUBLE_CHECK_PCT)

plot(strategy.position_size, "pos", display=display.data_window)
plot(tpLevel, "tp", display=display.data_window)
plot(slLevel, "sl", display=display.data_window)
